{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-33307","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-48110","text":"TRAAVIIS — Environment Authoring Closure ("},{"id":"spn-48111","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs init"},{"id":"spn-48112","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-48113","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs pack"},{"id":"spn-48114","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-33308","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48115","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date"},{"id":"spn-48116","text":" 2026-07-24 · "},{"id":"spn-48117","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status"},{"id":"spn-48118","text":" shipped, 34 new laws green, full suite green "},{"id":"spn-48119","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope"},{"id":"spn-48120","text":" RFC_TRAAVIIS_ARTIFACTS.md §5, §5a, §6 — the first two items of the deferred surface that §7's build order unblocks once "},{"id":"spn-48121","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-one"},{"id":"spn-48122","text":" exists."}]},{"id":"blk-33309","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-48123","text":"1. What shipped"}]},{"id":"blk-33310","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48124","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-one"},{"id":"spn-48125","text":" closed the beachhead: one agent, one frozen subject, one content-addressed receipt. But every bundle it could run had to be "},{"id":"spn-48126","marks":["italic"],"text":"hand-built"},{"id":"spn-48127","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-48128","marks":["code"],"text":"examples/eval-one/residency-forge/build_bundle.py"},{"id":"spn-48129","text":"). Authoring was the gap."}]},{"id":"blk-33311","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48130","text":"Two commands close it, and the split between them is the whole design:"}]},{"id":"blk-33312","kind":"code","language":"sh","text":"trvs init --list                                  # templates + their substrates\ntrvs init --template evidence-residency my-env    # seeds a subject + skeletons\ntrvs pack my-env my-env-pkg                       # closes it into a package\ntrvs eval-one my-env-pkg --agent … --platform linux-x86_64"},{"id":"blk-33313","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48131","text":"Verified end to end, from nothing to a scored episode:"}]},{"id":"blk-33314","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"init  →  8 files, identity: unresolved (init derives none)\npack  →  env-a38ec4c0…  snapshot snap-c66198ab…  task task-3b4b2599…\n         closure  ✓ verified before write\n         reopened ✓ re-derived from the written bytes\neval-one → status ✓ ok · validity valid · reward 1\n           citations pass · patch pass · tests pass · identity pass ·\n           finding_completeness pass"},{"id":"blk-33315","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48132","text":"The scaffolded residency subject recomputes to "},{"id":"spn-48133","marks":["bold"],"text":"exactly"},{"id":"spn-48134","text":" the frozen example's "},{"id":"spn-48135","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-c66198abf3ef6153d4bd6033fa40a0bd0028df3a7699ab645dc947710e51cba4"},{"id":"spn-48136","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-48137","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-25c4ce1276a7b70a473548354ae5d14f1c852ba087ffd09bc9b17b550c5c05a5"},{"id":"spn-48138","text":", and the "},{"id":"spn-48139","marks":["code"],"text":"golden-spinner"},{"id":"spn-48140","text":" template lowers to the frozen demo world "},{"id":"spn-48141","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-8ae91fe9cbc5fd086ce4356d…fe4a"},{"id":"spn-48142","text":". The seeds are the real artifacts, not lookalikes."}]},{"id":"blk-33316","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-48143","text":"2. The load-bearing decision: "},{"id":"spn-48144","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-48145","text":" derives nothing"}]},{"id":"blk-33317","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48146","text":"§6 says "},{"id":"spn-48147","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-48148","text":" \"invents no identity.\" Taken literally that forbids the obvious implementation — scaffolding a "},{"id":"spn-48149","marks":["code"],"text":"task.json"},{"id":"spn-48150","text":" with a "},{"id":"spn-48151","marks":["code"],"text":"reward_id"},{"id":"spn-48152","text":" in it — because a scaffold cannot know the hash of bytes the author has not written yet, and a placeholder hash is a lie that later verifies."}]},{"id":"blk-33318","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48153","text":"So the scaffold emits "},{"id":"spn-48154","marks":["bold"],"text":"references"},{"id":"spn-48155","text":", and packing is the substitution:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-33320","spans":[{"id":"spn-48156","text":"scaffold ("},{"id":"spn-48157","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-48158","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-33321","spans":[{"id":"spn-48159","text":"package ("},{"id":"spn-48160","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-48161","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-33319","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-33322","spans":[{"id":"spn-48162","marks":["code"],"text":"task.reward_spec: \"reward.json\""}]},{"id":"blk-33323","spans":[{"id":"spn-48163","marks":["code"],"text":"task.reward_id: \"rew-…\""}]}],[{"id":"blk-33324","spans":[{"id":"spn-48164","marks":["code"],"text":"subject.snapshot_def: \"snapshot_def.json\""}]},{"id":"blk-33325","spans":[{"id":"spn-48165","marks":["code"],"text":"subject.snapshot_id: \"snap-…\""}]}],[{"id":"blk-33326","spans":[{"id":"spn-48166","marks":["code"],"text":"identity_policy…"},{"id":"spn-48167","text":" "},{"id":"spn-48168","marks":["italic"],"text":"(no `before_id`)"}]},{"id":"blk-33327","spans":[{"id":"spn-48169","marks":["code"],"text":"before_id: \"sem-…\""},{"id":"spn-48170","text":" (lowered now)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33328","spans":[{"id":"spn-48171","marks":["italic"],"text":"(no `env_id`)"}]},{"id":"blk-33329","spans":[{"id":"spn-48172","marks":["code"],"text":"env_id: \"env-…\""}]}]]},{"id":"blk-33330","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48173","text":"That is why "},{"id":"spn-48174","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-48175","text":" needs no engine and "},{"id":"spn-48176","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-48177","text":" does. It also makes L1 mechanically checkable: "},{"id":"spn-48178","marks":["code"],"text":"scaffold.identity_violations()"},{"id":"spn-48179","text":" scans every emitted document for an identity "},{"id":"spn-48180","marks":["italic"],"text":"key"},{"id":"spn-48181","text":" at any depth "},{"id":"spn-48182","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-48183","text":" every emitted byte for an id-shaped literal, so a future template cannot quietly bake one in — including in prose."}]},{"id":"blk-33331","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48184","text":"The literal half fails "},{"id":"spn-48185","marks":["bold"],"text":"closed"},{"id":"spn-48186","text":". It used to be a "},{"id":"spn-48187","marks":["code"],"text":"<prefix>-[0-9a-f]{8,}"},{"id":"spn-48188","text":" regex, which matches a well-formed digest and "},{"id":"spn-48189","marks":["italic"],"text":"nothing else"},{"id":"spn-48190","text":": a rung-prefixed token it could not parse — "},{"id":"spn-48191","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-abcdef12ZZZ"},{"id":"spn-48192","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48193","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-ABCDEF1234567890"},{"id":"spn-48194","text":", or the same id under a changed grammar ("},{"id":"spn-48195","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-jcs1-…"},{"id":"spn-48196","text":") — produced no match, and a guard that finds no id reports no violation, so a typo and a scheme change both read as \"clean\". "},{"id":"spn-48197","marks":["code"],"text":"scaffold.id_tokens"},{"id":"spn-48198","text":" now recognises the "},{"id":"spn-48199","marks":["bold"],"text":"rung prefix first"},{"id":"spn-48200","text":" (from the one "},{"id":"spn-48201","marks":["code"],"text":"ID_RUNGS"},{"id":"spn-48202","text":" list, which "},{"id":"spn-48203","marks":["code"],"text":"test_scaffold"},{"id":"spn-48204","text":"'s L1c pins against the ids "},{"id":"spn-48205","marks":["code"],"text":"identity.py"},{"id":"spn-48206","text":" actually mints) and then asks whether the remainder is a digest. Three verdicts: "},{"id":"spn-48207","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-48208","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48209","marks":["code"],"text":"malformed"},{"id":"spn-48210","text":" (a known rung whose remainder does not parse) and "},{"id":"spn-48211","marks":["code"],"text":"unknown"},{"id":"spn-48212","text":" (a digest under a rung nobody should have minted). All three are violations. The elision form "},{"id":"spn-48213","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-48214","text":" is deliberately "},{"id":"spn-48215","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-48216","text":" a token — writing \"an id goes here\" asserts none."}]},{"id":"blk-33332","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-48217","text":"What the guard does not report, and why that is written down"}]},{"id":"blk-33333","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48218","text":"The first version of this rewrite claimed the three verdicts \"leave no token that is both id-shaped and unreported\". That sentence was false in "},{"id":"spn-48219","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-48220","text":" directions, and each direction is a way a guard stops guarding:"}]},{"id":"blk-33334","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33336","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48221","text":"It was "},{"id":"spn-48222","marks":["bold"],"text":"narrower than the regex it replaced"},{"id":"spn-48223","text":". A lookbehind refused to begin"}]}],"id":"blk-33335","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33337","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48224","text":"a token after "},{"id":"spn-48225","marks":["code"],"text":"-"},{"id":"spn-48226","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-48227","marks":["code"],"text":"."},{"id":"spn-48228","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-48229","marks":["code"],"text":"prev-episode-42d0bb07e5f83e9e"},{"id":"spn-48230","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-48231","marks":["code"],"text":"run.episode-42d0bb07e5f83e9e"},{"id":"spn-48232","text":" — which the old "},{"id":"spn-48233","marks":["code"],"text":"\\b"},{"id":"spn-48234","text":"-anchored regex reported — came back as "},{"id":"spn-48235","marks":["code"],"text":"[]"},{"id":"spn-48236","text":". A real, well-formed id, completely unreported. The lookbehind was standing in for something genuine ("},{"id":"spn-48237","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.finding- completeness-impl.v1"},{"id":"spn-48238","text":" is a declared verifier version present in every "},{"id":"spn-48239","marks":["code"],"text":"ComparisonV1"},{"id":"spn-48240","text":", and reading it as the "},{"id":"spn-48241","marks":["code"],"text":"finding"},{"id":"spn-48242","text":" rung failed "},{"id":"spn-48243","marks":["code"],"text":"test_compare"},{"id":"spn-48244","text":"'s C20), but it paid for that with coverage and no law recorded the trade."}]},{"id":"blk-33338","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33340","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48245","text":"It was "},{"id":"spn-48246","marks":["bold"],"text":"wider on prose"},{"id":"spn-48247","text":". Every hyphenated phrase whose first word happened"}]}],"id":"blk-33339","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33341","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48248","text":"to be a rung name — "},{"id":"spn-48249","marks":["code"],"text":"env-vars"},{"id":"spn-48250","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48251","marks":["code"],"text":"task-oriented"},{"id":"spn-48252","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48253","marks":["code"],"text":"patch-apply"},{"id":"spn-48254","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48255","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-ver"},{"id":"spn-48256","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48257","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-path"},{"id":"spn-48258","text":" — was reported as a malformed id. A guard that cries wolf is switched off by the next person to trip it, which is fail-open by a slower route. Swept over this repository plus its build artifacts and sealed bundles (~56,000 documents), the rewrite produced "},{"id":"spn-48259","marks":["bold"],"text":"419"},{"id":"spn-48260","text":" non-"},{"id":"spn-48261","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-48262","text":" verdicts where the current guard produces "},{"id":"spn-48263","marks":["bold"],"text":"29"},{"id":"spn-48264","text":". The ~60 distinct tokens it dropped are all prose or identifiers — "},{"id":"spn-48265","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-bundle"},{"id":"spn-48266","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48267","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-fixture"},{"id":"spn-48268","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48269","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-ver"},{"id":"spn-48270","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48271","marks":["code"],"text":"patch-fail"},{"id":"spn-48272","text":" — including "},{"id":"spn-48273","marks":["bold"],"text":"`task-b`, which appears in real packed `env.json` and `TRAAVIIS_BUNDLE.json` documents"},{"id":"spn-48274","text":": the rewrite called a task "},{"id":"spn-48275","marks":["italic"],"text":"filename"},{"id":"spn-48276","text":" a malformed id. What survives as "},{"id":"spn-48277","marks":["code"],"text":"malformed"},{"id":"spn-48278","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-48279","marks":["code"],"text":"*-PLACEHOLDER"},{"id":"spn-48280","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48281","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-abcdef12ZZZ"},{"id":"spn-48282","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48283","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-ABCDEF1234567890"},{"id":"spn-48284","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-48285","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-jcs1-…"},{"id":"spn-48286","text":" — every one an id-shaped token, and none of them prose."}]},{"id":"blk-33342","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48287","text":"The first defect is not visible as a count, and saying so is part of the record: committed text almost never writes an id inside a compound, which is exactly why nobody noticed it was no longer being read. It is demonstrated instead by planting — "},{"id":"spn-48288","marks":["code"],"text":"prev-episode-<64 hex>"},{"id":"spn-48289","text":" written into a real scaffolded template and into a real "},{"id":"spn-48290","marks":["code"],"text":"ComparisonV1"},{"id":"spn-48291","text":", where the legacy regex reports it, the rewrite reports nothing, and the current guard reports it again."}]},{"id":"blk-33343","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48292","text":"The discrimination that keeps both properties is the "},{"id":"spn-48293","marks":["bold"],"text":"remainder's shape"},{"id":"spn-48294","text":", with position gating only the "},{"id":"spn-48295","marks":["code"],"text":"malformed"},{"id":"spn-48296","text":" verdict and never the "},{"id":"spn-48297","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-48298","text":" one:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-33345","spans":[{"id":"spn-48299","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-33346","spans":[{"id":"spn-48300","text":"reported"}]}],"id":"blk-33344","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-33347","spans":[{"id":"spn-48301","text":"a well-formed digest, anywhere — "},{"id":"spn-48302","marks":["code"],"text":"prev-episode-<hex>"},{"id":"spn-48303","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48304","marks":["code"],"text":"run.episode-<hex>"}]},{"id":"blk-33348","spans":[{"id":"spn-48305","marks":["bold"],"text":"yes"},{"id":"spn-48306","text":", as "},{"id":"spn-48307","marks":["code"],"text":"id"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33349","spans":[{"id":"spn-48308","text":"a rung + a remainder bearing a digit, an uppercase letter, or a run ≥ 16"}]},{"id":"blk-33350","spans":[{"id":"spn-48309","marks":["bold"],"text":"yes"},{"id":"spn-48310","text":", as "},{"id":"spn-48311","marks":["code"],"text":"malformed"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33351","spans":[{"id":"spn-48312","text":"a rung + lowercase words of ordinary length — "},{"id":"spn-48313","marks":["code"],"text":"env-vars"},{"id":"spn-48314","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48315","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-nonsense"}]},{"id":"blk-33352","spans":[{"id":"spn-48316","text":"no"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33353","spans":[{"id":"spn-48317","text":"a rung "},{"id":"spn-48318","marks":["italic"],"text":"embedded"},{"id":"spn-48319","text":" in a compound name without a digest — "},{"id":"spn-48320","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.finding-completeness-impl.v1"},{"id":"spn-48321","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48322","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis-snap-01uu24ob"}]},{"id":"blk-33354","spans":[{"id":"spn-48323","text":"no"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-33355","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48324","text":"The third row is a "},{"id":"spn-48325","marks":["bold"],"text":"stated trade, not a discrimination"},{"id":"spn-48326","text":": "},{"id":"spn-48327","marks":["code"],"text":"nonsense"},{"id":"spn-48328","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-48329","marks":["code"],"text":"oriented"},{"id":"spn-48330","text":" are both eight lowercase letters with the same hex-letter density, and no lexical rule separates a typo'd id whose remainder happens to be word-shaped from an English phrase. What bounds the silence is that one edit in any direction — a digit, an uppercase letter, a longer run, an actual digest — puts the token back in scope. A mangled sha256 keeps its digits; a word has none. Both silences are pinned by "},{"id":"spn-48331","marks":["code"],"text":"test_scaffold"},{"id":"spn-48332","text":"'s "},{"id":"spn-48333","marks":["bold"],"text":"L1g"},{"id":"spn-48334","text":", and the boundary by "},{"id":"spn-48335","marks":["bold"],"text":"L1e"},{"id":"spn-48336","text":", so widening either has to move a law rather than a comment."}]},{"id":"blk-33356","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-48337","text":"3. "},{"id":"spn-48338","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-48339","text":" follows §6's order literally"}]},{"id":"blk-33357","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"1. validate_subject             well-formed for the profile\n2. recompute_subject_identity   snap-… / sem-… FROM THE BYTES\n3. bind + close                 rew-… → task-… → env-…\n4. verify_closure               every reference resolves\n--- nothing has been written yet ---\n5. write                        temp tree → one os.replace\n6. reopen_package               re-derive every id from what landed on disk"},{"id":"blk-33358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48340","text":"Step 6 is not ceremony. "},{"id":"spn-48341","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-48342","text":" deliberately does not trust its own in-memory computation: it reads the package back, re-derives "},{"id":"spn-48343","marks":["code"],"text":"env-"},{"id":"spn-48344","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-48345","marks":["code"],"text":"task-"},{"id":"spn-48346","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-48347","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-"},{"id":"spn-48348","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-48349","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-"},{"id":"spn-48350","text":" from the written bytes, "},{"id":"spn-48351","marks":["bold"],"text":"rebuilds the snapshot from the written subject tree"},{"id":"spn-48352","text":", and re-lowers the written world. If any of that disagrees, the package is removed and the command fails. Tampering with a packed task, or with one byte of a packed subject, is caught ("},{"id":"spn-48353","marks":["code"],"text":"REOPEN_TASK_ID"},{"id":"spn-48354","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48355","marks":["code"],"text":"REOPEN_SUBJECT_BYTES"},{"id":"spn-48356","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-33359","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48357","text":"Everything is fail-closed with a typed code: "},{"id":"spn-48358","marks":["code"],"text":"SOURCE_PREBOUND"},{"id":"spn-48359","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48360","marks":["code"],"text":"SUBJECT_DRIFT"},{"id":"spn-48361","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48362","marks":["code"],"text":"SUBJECT_KIND"},{"id":"spn-48363","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48364","marks":["code"],"text":"CLOSURE_VERIFIER"},{"id":"spn-48365","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48366","marks":["code"],"text":"CLOSURE_SUBJECT_BINDING"},{"id":"spn-48367","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48368","marks":["code"],"text":"SPLIT_UNRESOLVED"},{"id":"spn-48369","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48370","marks":["code"],"text":"DEST_NOT_EMPTY"},{"id":"spn-48371","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48372","marks":["code"],"text":"ENGINE_UNAVAILABLE"},{"id":"spn-48373","text":", "},{"id":"spn-48374","marks":["code"],"text":"REOPEN_*"},{"id":"spn-48375","text":". A refused pack writes nothing."}]},{"id":"blk-33360","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-48376","text":"4. The §5a admission interface is real"}]},{"id":"blk-33361","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48377","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/substrates.py"},{"id":"spn-48378","text":" implements "},{"id":"spn-48379","marks":["code"],"text":"validate_subject · verify_closure · recompute_subject_identity · reopen_package"},{"id":"spn-48380","text":" as a base class plus two profiles:"}]},{"id":"blk-33362","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33364","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48381","marks":["code"],"text":"trvm.world.v1"},{"id":"spn-48382","text":" — subject is WRL source; identity is "},{"id":"spn-48383","marks":["code"],"text":"engine.lower_source()"},{"id":"spn-48384","text":" →"}]}],"id":"blk-33363","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33365","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48385","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-48386","text":"; reopen re-lowers the written world."}]},{"id":"blk-33366","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48387","marks":["code"],"text":"residency.repository.v1"},{"id":"spn-48388","text":" — subject is a repository; identity is"}]}],"id":"blk-33367","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33369","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48389","marks":["code"],"text":"snapshot.build_snapshot()"},{"id":"spn-48390","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-48391","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-48392","text":"; reopen rebuilds it from the written tree; closure additionally checks the verifier plan is "},{"id":"spn-48393","marks":["italic"],"text":"answerable by the reward it is bound to"},{"id":"spn-48394","text":" and that the test plan declares a runner profile."}]},{"id":"blk-33370","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48395","text":"The packer branches on profile in exactly two places (which subject bytes to copy, and the eval-bundle emission). A third substrate is a new profile object, not a new branch — which was the point of §5a."}]},{"id":"blk-33371","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-48396","text":"5. Laws (34 new, all green)"}]},{"id":"blk-33372","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48397","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_scaffold.py"},{"id":"spn-48398","text":" — 16 laws: L1 invents no identity (incl. a planted-id detector test, so the check itself is proven to fire) · L2 deterministic (pure + on-disk) · L3 substrate-distinct · L4 declared frozen versions · L5 fail-closed + atomic (non-empty dest refused, mid-write failure leaves no partial tree and no temp dir) · L6 admissible input (snapshot definition matches the seeded tree exactly; both seeded worlds lower) · L7 portable (no absolute/host paths) · plus the CLI contract."}]},{"id":"blk-33373","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48399","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_pack.py"},{"id":"spn-48400","text":" — 18 laws: P1 every id recomputed, pre-bound ids refused · P2 content moves identity (subject bytes → "},{"id":"spn-48401","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-"},{"id":"spn-48402","text":"+"},{"id":"spn-48403","marks":["code"],"text":"env-"},{"id":"spn-48404","text":"; task instructions → "},{"id":"spn-48405","marks":["code"],"text":"task-"},{"id":"spn-48406","text":"+"},{"id":"spn-48407","marks":["code"],"text":"env-"},{"id":"spn-48408","text":") · "},{"id":"spn-48409","marks":["bold"],"text":"P3 presentation does NOT move `env-`"},{"id":"spn-48410","text":" (renaming + rewriting the description is byte-for-byte the same "},{"id":"spn-48411","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-48412","text":") · P4/P5 closure verified before write, nothing written on refusal, subject drift caught · P6 tampering fails reopen (task and subject) · P7 "},{"id":"spn-48413","marks":["code"],"text":"before_id"},{"id":"spn-48414","text":" is computed, and a declared one is refused · P8 determinism · P9 the TRVM profile lowers + reopens, and is a typed failure with no engine · P10 the packed environment actually runs to reward 1.0."}]},{"id":"blk-33374","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48415","text":"Regression: full suite green — identity 25, snapshot 10, reward 17, admission 16, paths 10, execfacts 8, vcontext 5, patchapply 10, verifiers 15, runner 10, evalone 14, substrate_verifiers 24, forge_adapter 6, cli_evalone 18, real_residency 9, episode_evidence 56."}]},{"id":"blk-33375","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-48416","text":"6. Autonomous decisions — flagged for GPT-5.6"}]},{"id":"blk-33376","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33378","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48417","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scaffold-level references + `residency.snapshot-def.v1`."},{"id":"spn-48418","text":" §5 names a"}]}],"id":"blk-33377","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-33379","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48419","text":"\"snapshot definition\" as the scaffolded residency artifact; I gave it its own version string rather than emitting a "},{"id":"spn-48420","marks":["code"],"text":"residency.snapshot.v1"},{"id":"spn-48421","text":" with empty hashes. Confirm the name."}]},{"id":"blk-33380","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33382","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48422","marks":["bold"],"text":"`env-` identity allowlist excludes `name` and `description`."},{"id":"spn-48423","text":" §5 says"}]}],"id":"blk-33381","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-33383","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48424","text":"presentation-only edits move "},{"id":"spn-48425","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-48426","text":" only, so this is implemented as an explicit allowlist (like "},{"id":"spn-48427","marks":["code"],"text":"canonicalize_episode"},{"id":"spn-48428","text":") rather than by convention. Confirm "},{"id":"spn-48429","marks":["code"],"text":"name"},{"id":"spn-48430","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-48431","marks":["code"],"text":"description"},{"id":"spn-48432","text":" are presentation."}]},{"id":"blk-33384","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33386","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48433","marks":["bold"],"text":"`bundle-…` is not implemented."},{"id":"spn-48434","text":" "},{"id":"spn-48435","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-48436","text":" emits a package "},{"id":"spn-48437","marks":["italic"],"text":"directory"},{"id":"spn-48438","text":" and an"}]}],"id":"blk-33385","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-33387","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48439","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-48440","text":"; the outer content-addressed distributed package id from D3 is still open. This is the remaining half of §5 and I did not invent it."}]},{"id":"blk-33388","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33390","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48441","marks":["bold"],"text":"Single-task residency packages also emit `bundle.json`"},{"id":"spn-48442","text":" so "},{"id":"spn-48443","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-48444","text":" output is"}]}],"id":"blk-33389","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-33391","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48445","text":"directly runnable by "},{"id":"spn-48446","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-one"},{"id":"spn-48447","text":". Multi-task packages do "},{"id":"spn-48448","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-48449","text":" get one (they would need a split-runner, i.e. "},{"id":"spn-48450","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval"},{"id":"spn-48451","text":") — deferred rather than emitted half-true."}]},{"id":"blk-33392","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33394","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48452","marks":["bold"],"text":"`pack` soft-loads the engine."},{"id":"spn-48453","text":" "},{"id":"spn-48454","marks":["code"],"text":"ENGINE_UNAVAILABLE"},{"id":"spn-48455","text":" is a typed admission"}]}],"id":"blk-33393","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":5},{"id":"blk-33395","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48456","text":"failure, so a residency pack that needs no lowering still works on a machine with no TRVM checkout."}]},{"id":"blk-33396","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33398","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48457","marks":["bold"],"text":"`RemoveObject`-style non-cascading discipline kept"},{"id":"spn-48458","text":": "},{"id":"spn-48459","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-48460","text":" never repairs a"}]}],"id":"blk-33397","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":6},{"id":"blk-33399","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48461","text":"scaffold. Subject drift is an error, not an auto-sync."}]},{"id":"blk-33400","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-48462","text":"7. Not built (deferred, per ruling)"}]},{"id":"blk-33401","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48463","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval"},{"id":"spn-48464","text":" (splits), "},{"id":"spn-48465","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs serve --ors/--mcp"},{"id":"spn-48466","text":" (adapters over the Episode Kernel), "},{"id":"spn-48467","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-48468","text":", and the REPL. §7's order puts "},{"id":"spn-48469","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-48470","text":" next; "},{"id":"spn-48471","marks":["code"],"text":"serve"},{"id":"spn-48472","text":" needs the D5 process model, which is specified but unbuilt."}]},{"id":"blk-33402","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-48473","text":"MIT licensed · TRAAVIIS Holdings · part of the [&] Protocol ecosystem."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierapal3zgozhsuwxjvsbelhzitp77uj3ml3wmm7tctv523muugihawa","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}